# NEVER upload the runtime store — it holds scrypt password hashes and
# real customer addresses. It is gitignored, but `vercel` uploads the
# working directory, so a local data/ from `node server.js` would other-
# wise be published. This line is the thing standing between a test run
# and a public password-hash dump.
data/

# Docs and other hosts' config — no reason to ship them.
README.md
CLAUDE.md
.netlify/
.git/
